                    <death when="1833-09-23"/>
                    <occupation>barrister</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Losh was an reformer and philanthropist with wide literary interests. He campaigned for Catholic empancipation and the abolition of the slave trade. He
    was friends with <persName key="WOR01">Wordsworth</persName>, <persName key="COL01">Coleridge</persName>, and <persName key="SOU01">Southey</persName>. 
      Godwin sees him at <persName key="MAC01">Mackintosh's</persName>, <persName key="PAR03">Parr's</persName>, and others, and in 1798 meets him and sees him several times 
    in Bath. Losh moved to Newcastle in 1799.</p>
                    </note>
